cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  The Single-Creator Trap: Preliminary Findings from a
  Prospective Cold-Start Case Study
message: >-
  If you use this dataset or report, please cite it as below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Chanmin
    family-names: Kim
    affiliation: Eliary Inc.
    email: chanmin@eliary.com
abstract: >-
  Preliminary findings from a prospective real-time case
  study of cold-start dynamics on a question-and-answer
  social platform launched March 29, 2026 to a single
  content creator's audience. Defines the Single-Creator
  Trap and the Creator Concentration Index (CCI). Reports
  Phase 1 baseline (April 1–April 15, 2026): DAU collapse
  from 114 to 7, CCI ≥ 0.5 on most days, D-7 retention 7.3%
  on the largest invite cohort, and zero friendship-formation
  events across 291 signups in 21 days. Phase 2 (intervention)
  and Phase 3 (creator silence test) are under active
  analysis; full manuscript in preparation for ICWSM 2027.
keywords:
  - cold start
  - platform economics
  - creator economy
  - network effects
  - social networks
  - prospective case study
  - influencer launch
